    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 31st with a focus on exploiting favorable matchups against higher-xERA arms, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (75.43) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32). **Junior Caminero** projects as our most efficient bat of the day, capitalizing on a weak 5.17 xERA from Kochanowicz, while **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill context against Imai and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates him into elite territory. **Colt Keith** (64.31) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) also provide high-floor production; **Casey Schmitt** is particularly interesting today as his lead-off spot against Gordon provides a unique synergy with his dynamic platoon profile and a park factor boost, while his active base-running profile makes him a rare asset in our scarce SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Chase Meidroth** (53.67) on the bench. While his score is respectable, he ultimately fell short of the high-leverage utility spots occupied by **Luke Raley** and **Yordan Alvarez**, whose xwOBA metrics remain too potent to exclude despite challenging matchups. We are keeping a close watch on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (59.04); his projected efficiency remains solid, but his status is contingent on a pending lineup announcement. Should he slide down the order, his utility diminishes rapidly against Liberatore. Conversely, we must be wary of **Trea Turner** (49.97) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.17) today; both face top-tier arms in Yamamoto and Bradish, respectively, whose elite SP skills significantly dampen their raw projection scores and suppress their typical ceiling in the 5x5 format.",
